{%- comment -%}
Parses one recorded time into seconds.

`time` is a race clock: three parts are h:mm:ss, two are mm:ss — the usual
convention, so "1:53:23" is a half and "22:15" is a 5k. `duration_min` is the
fallback for something timed only to the minute.

A time must be quoted in the YAML. Left bare, Ruby's parser reads 1:53:23 as
the integer 6803 and 22:15 as 80100 (22 h 15 m), so a value with no colon is
refused rather than guessed at: parsed_sec stays 0 and parsed_unquoted is set
for the caller to show.

Sets, for the caller: parsed_sec, parsed_precise, parsed_unquoted. The working names clock,
clock_h, clock_m and clock_s leak too, since Jekyll includes share the caller's
scope.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign parsed_sec = 0 -%}
{%- assign parsed_precise = false -%}
{%- assign parsed_unquoted = false -%}

{%- if include.time -%}
  {%- assign clock = include.time | split: ":" -%}
  {%- if clock.size >= 3 -%}
    {%- assign clock_h = clock[0] | times: 3600 -%}
    {%- assign clock_m = clock[1] | times: 60 -%}
    {%- assign clock_s = clock[2] | times: 1 -%}
    {%- assign parsed_sec = clock_h | plus: clock_m | plus: clock_s -%}
    {%- assign parsed_precise = true -%}
  {%- elsif clock.size == 2 -%}
    {%- assign clock_m = clock[0] | times: 60 -%}
    {%- assign clock_s = clock[1] | times: 1 -%}
    {%- assign parsed_sec = clock_m | plus: clock_s -%}
    {%- assign parsed_precise = true -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign parsed_unquoted = true -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- elsif include.duration_min -%}
  {%- assign parsed_sec = include.duration_min | times: 60 | round -%}
{%- endif -%}
